// === MINIMAL REPRO: Compiler native-stack overflow during generic monomorphization ===
//
// Toolchain: ~/Projects/Vyb/build/vyb @ 55593fc
// Run:       <vyb> mini_map_repro.vyb          (exit 139, SIGSEGV at COMPILE time)
//
// Instantiating TWO DIFFERENT generic HashMap types in one program makes the
// JIT (LLVMCodegen) overflow the native stack while codegen'ing the HashMap
// ctor (monomorphizeGenericFunction("__ctor_HashMap_0")). EACH ALONE compiles
// fine:
//   - mini_map_A.vyb : HashMap<String, Int> only                      -> exit 0
//   - mini_map_B.vyb : HashMap<Int, String> only                      -> exit 0
//   - mini_map_repro : both in one program (this file)                -> SIGSEGV 3/3
//
// gdb backtrace (crash is in the COMPILER, not in user code):
//   LLVMCodegen::visit(CallExpression)  cgen_expr.cpp:1357
//     -> ConstructionExpression::accept (ast.cpp:398)
//       -> VariableDeclaration::accept  (ast.cpp:1128)
//         -> BlockStatement::accept     (ast.cpp:517)
//           -> monomorphizeGenericFunction("__ctor_HashMap_0")
//   ... (25+ identical frames, recursively nesting) ...
//   Program received signal SIGSEGV; rsp=0x7fffff7fef68 (main thread 8MB
//   stack limit at ~0x7fffff800000) -> native stack overflow, not a runaway.
//
// Impact on VybForge: the Qwen tokenizer's encode() (HashMap<String,Int>
// vocab) and decode_ids() (HashMap<Int,String> reverse-vocab) are each
// correct standalone (encode 13/13 vs transformers; decode round-trips
// exactly). But a program that uses BOTH — i.e. the real encode->decode
// pipeline — crashes the compiler before running. Not a workaround; needs a
// compiler fix (bounded/incremental monomorphization or a larger/JIT work-stack).
import collections
share(all) build_vocab2()<HashMap<String, Int>> -> {
    m<HashMap<String, Int>> = HashMap<String, Int>()
    m.put("a", 1)
    return m
}
share(all) build_rev2()<HashMap<Int, String>> -> {
    m<HashMap<Int, String>> = HashMap<Int, String>()
    m.put(1, "a")
    return m
}
main()<Int> -> {
    v<HashMap<String, Int>> = build_vocab2()
    r<HashMap<Int, String>> = build_rev2()
    println_int(v.get("a") else -1)
    println(r.get(1) else "?")
    return 0
}
